# Sources for searched replies: April 2006 UCI specification https://backscattering.de/chess/uci/
# (info and bestmove), fisher-2aj rules 1, 7 and 10, and python-chess 1.11.2
# for the independently checked exact values. Written 2026-11-23.
# Sources: April 2006 UCI specification https://backscattering.de/chess/uci/
# and fisher-l7f owner decisions. Written 2026-11-22.
# Exact replies and legal move sequences verified with python-chess 1.11.2.
# UCI position and move format. e5d6 is en passant, and e1g1 castles.
> position startpos moves e2e4 a7a6 e4e5 d7d5 e5d6 e7e6 g1f3 g8f6 f1e2 f8e7 e1g1
> go
# Rules 1 and 10. UCI info depth, score and nodes.
< info depth 4 score {score} nodes {nodes}
# UCI bestmove. The reply carries a legal move in the current position.
< bestmove {legal}
# UCI position and move format. The castling rook leaves the h-file.
> position fen 8/6k1/6B1/3B4/5Q2/8/6R1/4K2R w K - 0 1 moves e1g1
> go
# Rules 1 and 10. UCI info depth, score and nodes.
< info depth 4 score {score} nodes {nodes}
# The only legal reply fails if the castling rook still attacks h8.
< bestmove g7h8
# UCI position. The en passant capture makes d5 available to the black king.
> position fen 8/8/5B2/3pP1K1/4k3/8/5Q2/4N3 w - d6 0 1 moves e5d6
> go
# Rules 1 and 10. UCI info depth, score and nodes.
< info depth 4 score {score} nodes {nodes}
# The only legal reply fails if the captured pawn stays on d5.
< bestmove e4d5
# UCI position and move format. The pawn promotes to a knight.
> position fen 3Q4/P7/k7/3K4/8/1R6/8/8 w - - 0 1 moves a7a8n
> go
# Rules 1 and 10. UCI info depth, score and nodes.
< info depth 4 score {score} nodes {nodes}
# The only legal reply fails if the promotion creates a queen.
< bestmove a6a7
# The next move requires a knight on a8. A bishop cannot reach b6.
> position fen 3Q4/P7/k7/3K4/8/1R6/8/8 w - - 0 1 moves a7a8n a6a7 a8b6
> go
# Rules 1 and 10. UCI info depth, score and nodes.
< info depth 4 score {score} nodes {nodes}
# Black can play either a7a6 or a7b7 after the full replay.
< bestmove {legal}
> position fen 8/P7/8/8/8/6q1/5k2/7K w - - 0 1
> go
# Rules 1 and 10. UCI info depth, score and nodes.
< info depth 4 score {score} nodes {nodes}
# UCI move format and bestmove. Every legal move has a promotion suffix.
< bestmove {legal}
> position fen 7k/8/5K1Q/8/8/8/8/8 b - - 0 1
# The owner accepts an empty moves list as zero moves in fisher-l7f.7.
> position startpos moves
> go
# Rules 1, 2, 5, 7 and 10. The published starting-position perft counts
# in expectations/perft.epd sum to 206603. Python-chess confirms cp 0.
< info depth 4 score cp 0 nodes 206603
# The starting position replaces the prior position, whose only move is h8g8.
< bestmove {legal}
> position fen 7k/8/5K2/6Q1/8/8/8/8 b - - 0 1 moves
> go
# Rules 4, 5, 7 and 10. Black must play h8h7, then g5g7 is checkmate.
# Python-chess counts 1, 25, 45 and 1228 nodes at plies 1 to 4.
< info depth 4 score mate -1 nodes 1299
# The owner accepts an empty list after FEN too. This position has one legal move.
< bestmove h8h7
> position startpos
> go
# Rules 1, 2, 5, 7 and 10. The published starting-position perft counts
# in expectations/perft.epd sum to 206603. Python-chess confirms cp 0.
< info depth 4 score cp 0 nodes 206603
# The starting position replaces the prior position, whose only move is h8h7.
< bestmove {legal}
# UCI quit.
> quit
! exit
